-- title:
--   At the cusp of the level-one j-line, ord is the q-adic order
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field. Inside the field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k$ of formal Laurent series over $k$, consider the intermediate field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC } k\ 1$, the $k$-subfield generated by the two series $\mathtt{jqModC } k$ and $\mathtt{jqNModC } k\ 1$, where $\mathtt{jqModC } k = q^{-1}\cdot \mathtt{jNum}$ is the image in $k$-coefficients of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}+744+\dots$ (the monomial $q^{-1}$ times the power series $\mathtt{jNum}$, whose constant term is $1$), and $\mathtt{jqNModC } k\ 1$ is its level-$1$ reindexing. Let $\mathtt{placeInfty } k$ be the place of $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,k$ over $k$ whose valuation subring is that of the infinite valuation $\mathtt{RatFunc.inftyValuation } k$, and transport it along the $k$-algebra isomorphism $\mathtt{ratFuncEquivCharLOneC } k : \mathrm{RatFunc}\,k \simeq \mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC } k\ 1$ sending the rational-function variable to $\mathtt{jqModC } k$, using $\mathtt{charLGeomPlaceEquiv } k$. The assertion is that for every element $g$ of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC } k\ 1$, the order of $g$ at this transported place, namely $-\log$ of the value of the associated adic valuation, equals the Hahn-series order of $g$ viewed as an element of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k$ (both sides being $0$ for $g = 0$ by convention).
--
--   This is the cusp dictionary for the level-one modular function field: the place obtained by pulling back the place at infinity of the rational function field along the $j$-coordinate computes the $q$-adic order of vanishing of a $q$-expansion. It is used in the construction of charts and cusp laws for models of modular curves, where orders of vanishing at the cusp must be read off from $q$-expansions.
